                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>"Nursing Ethics" is a compulsory undergraduate nursing course that systematically introduces the theoretical foundations, basic principles, clinical ethical standards and decision-making in nursing ethics. It covers topics including patient rights, organ transplantation, assisted reproduction, palliative care, and research ethics. The course focuses on cultivating students' ethical reasoning abilities, humanistic care spirit, and professional moral literacy, guiding them to prioritize patient interests and fulfill their ethical responsibilities in clinical practice.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
